 ## Overview
-Null-Scattering Volumetric Path Tracing is an unbiased algorithm for rendering participating media that uses a homogeneous majorant medium with an added null-scattering term to sample distances along a ray [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently sampling interaction points in sparse or heterogeneous media by treating absorption, scattering, and null-scattering as mutually exclusive events with probabilities proportional to their coefficients [S1]. It differs from standard delta tracking by explicitly maintaining a majorant transmittance factor $T_{maj}$ and applying Russian Roulette based on the ratio of null density to the majorant, ensuring unbiased estimates even when the majorant significantly overestimates the physical extinction [S1]. It builds on the [Null-Scattering Path Integral Framework](3070-null-scattering-path-integral-framework.md).
