 **Pitfalls:**
-*   The majorant $\sigma_{maj}$ is often piecewise-constant along a ray. The transmittance $T_{maj}$ is continuous but has discontinuous first derivatives at segment boundaries. Sampling must account for these segments by updating $\sigma_{maj}$ and $T_{maj}$ correctly at each segment transition [S1].
-*   If $\sigma_{maj}$ is not constant, the simple exponential sampling $p(t) = \sigma_{maj} e^{-\sigma_{maj} t}$ is invalid across segment boundaries. The algorithm must sample within the current segment and handle transitions explicitly [S1].
