 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Null-Scattering Extension](4371-null-scattering-extension.md)
-Generalizes the equation of transfer to enable unbiased sampling from a modified transmittance equation using a constant majorant extinction coefficient. Solves efficient sampling in sparse/heterogeneous media by homogenizing density. Differs from standard delta tracking by maintaining $T_{maj}$ and applying Russian Roulette based on null density ratio.
+Generalizes the equation of transfer to enable unbiased sampling from a modified transmittance equation using a constant majorant extinction coefficient. Solves efficient sampling in sparse or heterogeneous media by homogenizing density. Differs from standard delta tracking by maintaining $T_{maj}$ and applying Russian Roulette based on null density ratio. Choose when media density varies significantly along rays and standard tracking becomes inefficient.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear in the number of scattering events, which depends on the optical thickness and the ratio of physical extinction to majorant. Higher $\sigma_{maj}$ leads to more null-scattering events and longer paths.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Linear in the path length due to recursion.
-*   **Strengths:** Unbiased, handles heterogeneous media efficiently via majorant sampling, simple implementation.
-*   **Limitations:** Performance degrades if $\sigma_{maj}$ is much larger than physical extinction (high null-scattering rate). Requires accurate majorant computation.
-*   **When to Use:** Sparse or heterogeneous media where standard delta tracking is inefficient or inaccurate.
-*   **When Not to Use:** Dense media where $\sigma_{maj}$ is close to physical extinction, or when performance is critical and bias is acceptable.
